# XCU bc
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# All tests run in the POSIX locale with the standard input a pipe that ends,
# so bc is never interactive. Fractions below one are accepted with or
# without the leading zero, which the page leaves unspecified.

assertion  XCU.bc.001
anchor     utilities/bc.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/bc.html#STDOUT
anchor     utilities/bc.html#EXIT STATUS
class      required
since      1992
says       Integer expressions are evaluated exactly with the stated operators, precedence and associativity, each expression that is not an assignment is written on its own line, and the status is 0 on success.
test       t/001-arithmetic.sh

assertion  XCU.bc.002
anchor     utilities/bc.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1992
says       scale limits the fractional digits kept (truncating, not rounding), and the scale of results follows the rules for constants, sums, products, remainders, sqrt, length and scale().
test       t/002-scale.sh

assertion  XCU.bc.003
anchor     utilities/bc.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1992
says       ibase and obase select the radix of input and output; a single digit assigned to either is hexadecimal; bases above 16 write space-led multi-digit decimal numbers.
test       t/003-bases.sh

assertion  XCU.bc.004
anchor     utilities/bc.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1992
says       Identifiers and array elements start at zero, the three name classes do not conflict, subscripts are truncated, and ++, -- and compound assignments behave as described.
test       t/004-variables-and-arrays.sh

assertion  XCU.bc.005
anchor     utilities/bc.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1992
says       if, while, for, break and quit work, relational operators are valid in them, strings are written as given, comments have no effect, and statements run in sequence.
test       t/005-control-flow-strings-comments.sh

assertion  XCU.bc.006
anchor     utilities/bc.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1992
says       Functions take parameters by value (arrays by name), have auto locals, return a value or zero, may recurse, are replaced on redefinition, and names refer to the newest binding.
test       t/006-functions.sh

assertion  XCU.bc.007
anchor     utilities/bc.html#OPTIONS/-l
anchor     utilities/bc.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1992
says       With -l scale starts at 20 and s, c, a, l, e and j are defined, return results at the current scale and leave scale unchanged.
test       t/007-math-library.sh

assertion  XCU.bc.008
anchor     utilities/bc.html#OPERANDS/file
anchor     utilities/bc.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/bc.html#INPUT FILES
class      required
since      1992
says       bc executes each file operand in order, then the standard input.
test       t/008-files-and-stdin.sh

assertion  XCU.bc.009
anchor     utilities/bc.html#CONSEQUENCES OF ERRORS
class      required
since      1992
says       A file operand that cannot be accessed gets a diagnostic and ends bc without further action.
test       t/009-missing-file.sh

assertion  XCU.bc.010
anchor     utilities/bc.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1992
says       Very long numbers are folded into lines of at most 70 characters of the number (and the backslash), each continued line ending with a backslash.
test       t/010-long-numbers.sh
